vbMark wrote:
> 
> Can someone please explain to me what a bones file is and what it is used 
> for.  And the same with Hearse?

Bones files may be created by Nethack if a character dies (if some other
conditions[1] apply it's a 1-in-4 chance, AFAIR). The bones file contains
a ghost (or zombie or mummie?) of the former adventurer standing on top
of his pile of items that he carried; the items are mainly cursed. The
level is otherwise as it had been left; the creatures that killed this
adventurers are still around, shops might have been plundered, you may
find engravings, walls dug, etc. Whenever some character enters a level
where the above conditions apply[2] a previously created bones level may
be loaded.

Hearse is some file exchange method where people who are usually playing
in their local environment exchange their bones files to see a bit of
the environment of other players, have surprises, or tease the others by
uploading horrible bones files for the unaware.

Janis

[1] Must be at least dungeon level 5 and some special levels are excluded.

[2] Strictly speaking it is a bit more complex, there are special cases...


